WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.875
<b>In the previous verses,</b>

2
00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:33.916
<b>Lord Krishna explained about </b>
<b>those great individuals</b>

3
00:00:33.916 --> 00:00:40.083
<b>who, whether spiritually perfect or </b>
<b>without any worldly desires,</b>

4
00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:45.666
<b>never abandon the path of duty.</b>

5
00:00:45.666 --> 00:00:49.583
<b>They follow the path of karma solely</b>
<b>to set an example for others. </b>

6
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:54.083
<b>To establish a model for people to follow, </b>
<b>for the welfare of the masses,</b>

7
00:00:54.083 --> 00:01:07.291
<b>and to inspire everyone on the right path of karma </b>
<b>yoga, they themselves walk on this path of action.</b>

8
00:01:07.291 --> 00:01:11.958
<b>Now, Lord Krishna is giving his </b>
<b>own personal example.</b>

9
00:01:16.666 --> 00:01:19.291
<b>Lord Krishna tells Arjuna,</b>

10
00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:20.541
<b>"O Partha,</b>

11
00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:24.916
<b> in all three worlds, there is </b>
<b>no duty left for me to perform,</b>

12
00:01:24.916 --> 00:01:29.916
<b>nor is there anything I wish to attain.</b>

13
00:01:29.916 --> 00:01:35.208
<b>Yet, I diligently fulfill my duties."</b>

14
00:01:35.208 --> 00:01:36.458
<b>Usually,</b>

15
00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:44.500
<b>we perform our duties to fulfill a desire </b>
<b>or to honor our commitments to others.</b>

16
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.333
<b>But</b>

17
00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:49.333
<b>Lord Krishna is divine; these things</b>
<b>don't apply to him.</b>

18
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:52.750
<b>He has no desires or obligations,</b>

19
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:57.125
<b>yet to guide the world in the right direction</b>

20
00:01:57.125 --> 00:02:02.666
<b>and to set a proper example, </b>
<b>he carries out his duties.</b>

21
00:02:02.666 --> 00:02:04.125
<b>In the coming chapters,</b>

22
00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:05.791
<b>Lord Krishna will explain</b>

23
00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:12.000
<b>that he incarnates in this world solely to </b>
<b>establish the principles of dharma.</b>

24
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.041
<b>Here, the context of dharma must be understood.</b>

25
00:02:15.041 --> 00:02:22.666
<b>Dharma means living life according to </b>
<b>the right values, ethics, and ideals.</b>

26
00:02:22.666 --> 00:02:23.625
<b>Also,</b>

27
00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:28.958
<b>understand how Lord Krishna </b>
<b>is re-establishing dharma.</b>

28
00:02:28.958 --> 00:02:32.791
<b>He is doing so by imparting </b>
<b>the teachings of the Gita,</b>

29
00:02:32.791 --> 00:02:35.416
<b>by living in this world himself,</b>

30
00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:41.125
<b>and by setting an example for others through </b>
<b>the performance of his duties.</b>

31
00:02:41.125 --> 00:02:45.833
<b>Here, for the first time, Lord Krishna </b>
<b>hints at his divine status.</b>

32
00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:52.250
<b>By stating that he has no remaining duties </b>
<b>or things to attain in the three worlds,</b>

33
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:56.000
<b>it's an indirect indication to Arjuna</b>

34
00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:03.458
<b>that if the Lord himself is standing by </b>
<b>his side as a charioteer, fulfilling his duty,</b>

35
00:03:03.458 --> 00:03:06.541
<b>then why should Arjuna back down?</b>

36
00:03:06.541 --> 00:03:07.750
<b>This is a hint</b>

37
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:15.375
<b>that Arjuna should also follow this example </b>
<b>and fully carry out his duties.</b>

38
00:03:20.125 --> 00:03:28.083
<b>What usually motivates us to take action ?</b>

39
00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:31.333
<b>There can be many reasons.</b>

40
00:03:31.333 --> 00:03:32.666
<b>Firstly,</b>

41
00:03:32.666 --> 00:03:35.083
<b>basic necessities</b>

42
00:03:35.083 --> 00:03:37.041
<b>like food,</b>

43
00:03:37.041 --> 00:03:37.916
<b>clothing,</b>

44
00:03:37.916 --> 00:03:39.583
<b>shelter etc.</b>

45
00:03:39.583 --> 00:03:46.791
<b>Education for children is also an</b>
<b>example of these basic needs.</b>

46
00:03:46.791 --> 00:03:52.666
<b>Often our actions are also driven by desires –</b>

47
00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:54.208
<b>for instance,</b>

48
00:03:54.208 --> 00:03:57.750
<b>buying a big house or car,</b>

49
00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:03.583
<b>or the desire to travel abroad on vacation,</b>

50
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:08.250
<b>and many other such wishes.</b>

51
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.916
<b>These need</b>

52
00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:19.166
<b>and desires motivate us to work hard </b>
<b>and advance in our professional lives.</b>

53
00:04:19.166 --> 00:04:20.416
<b>But</b>

54
00:04:20.416 --> 00:04:27.500
<b>can our work be limited to just </b>
<b>fulfilling these wants and needs?</b>

55
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:33.625
<b>Can you live isolated from society,</b>
<b>from others in the world?</b>

56
00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:35.375
<b>No, right?</b>

57
00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:41.416
<b>We are all living lives that are </b>
<b>interdependent on each other.</b>

58
00:04:41.416 --> 00:04:42.875
<b>Therefore,</b>

59
00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:45.291
<b>it becomes essential</b>

60
00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:51.000
<b>to also consider how you are</b>
<b>fulfilling your duty towards society.</b>

61
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.708
<b>This can also be viewed in terms of</b>
<b>how whatever work you do</b>

62
00:04:56.708 --> 00:05:01.958
<b>benefits someone or the other.</b>

63
00:05:01.958 --> 00:05:06.458
<b>This awareness gives you a </b>
<b>different perspective in your profession.</b>

64
00:05:06.458 --> 00:05:10.333
<b>It makes you conscious </b>
<b>of your social contribution.</b>

65
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:11.416
<b>However,</b>

66
00:05:11.416 --> 00:05:15.625
<b>if you want to progress in the </b>
<b>direction of spiritual upliftment,</b>

67
00:05:15.625 --> 00:05:17.125
<b>you must consider –</b>

68
00:05:17.125 --> 00:05:25.500
<b>if all your needs and desires </b>
<b>were fulfilled without any effort,</b>

69
00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:29.833
<b>would you renounce all actions?</b>

70
00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:33.541
<b>This question may confuse you.</b>

71
00:05:33.541 --> 00:05:37.333
<b>Your mind may say</b>

72
00:05:37.333 --> 00:05:45.291
<b>what is the need for hard work or </b>
<b>fulfilling any duty in such a comfortable life.</b>

73
00:05:45.291 --> 00:05:47.541
<b>But the truth is,</b>

74
00:05:47.541 --> 00:05:55.125
<b>your contentment will only last if you </b>
<b>contribute something to society.</b>

75
00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:56.166
<b>Otherwise,</b>

76
00:05:56.166 --> 00:05:59.541
<b>life will quickly become dull.</b>

77
00:05:59.541 --> 00:06:04.250
<b>Understand this secret to a satisfied life.</b>

78
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:10.958
<b>Many such secrets will be revealed</b>
<b>to you through this Gita.</b>

79
00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:13.083
<b>Stay tuned.</b>

80
00:06:13.083 --> 00:06:14.791
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

81
00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:25.375
<b>We often see in our families and social situations</b>

82
00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:30.041
<b>that some people don't show interest </b>
<b>in doing their work</b>

83
00:06:30.041 --> 00:06:34.958
<b>because they feel there is no excitement in it,</b>

84
00:06:34.958 --> 00:06:39.958
<b>or that they will gain no benefit from it.</b>

85
00:06:39.958 --> 00:06:41.375
<b>For example,</b>

86
00:06:41.375 --> 00:06:49.833
<b>caring for dependent elders is a</b>
<b>task that may not have any particular gain,</b>

87
00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:52.750
<b>nor is it an exciting task,</b>

88
00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:53.875
<b>but</b>

89
00:06:53.875 --> 00:07:00.208
<b>it is still an extremely important </b>
<b>duty for a healthy society –</b>

90
00:07:00.208 --> 00:07:04.625
<b>that those elders who made many contributions</b>

91
00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:11.041
<b>and fulfilled responsibilities in their lifetimes, </b>
<b>are also well cared for at this age.</b>

92
00:07:11.041 --> 00:07:12.375
<b>Now think about this –</b>

93
00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:18.500
<b>if everyone only thinks of excitement and gain,</b>

94
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:24.291
<b>then a day will come when</b>
<b>you yourself may be elderly,</b>

95
00:07:24.291 --> 00:07:29.083
<b>and there will be no one to help you.</b>

96
00:07:29.083 --> 00:07:33.958
<b>It is necessary that we perform our duties, </b>
<b>not only for profit</b>

97
00:07:33.958 --> 00:07:38.291
<b>but also some actions for social contribution.</b>

98
00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:42.500
<b>Caring for the environment, </b>
<b>nurturing orphaned children,</b>

99
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.250
<b>education for children from</b>
<b>underprivileged families –</b>

100
00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:52.083
<b>these are many examples of </b>
<b>how you can make social contributions.</b>

101
00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:56.875
<b>This sense of responsibility is </b>
<b>not only necessary for social order,</b>

102
00:07:56.875 --> 00:08:02.208
<b>but such selfless deeds, rising above desires,</b>

103
00:08:02.208 --> 00:08:08.125
<b>will also give you an experience of</b>
<b>immense fulfillment in life.</b>

104
00:08:08.125 --> 00:08:14.041
<b>Think about what contributions </b>
<b>you can make in this direction.</b>

105
00:08:14.041 --> 00:08:16.041
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

106
00:08:20.791 --> 00:08:23.375
<b>Think about it –</b>

107
00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:29.958
<b>does earning a salary alone </b>
<b>motivate you to do your work?</b>

108
00:08:29.958 --> 00:08:32.416
<b>If only the salary keeps increasing,</b>

109
00:08:32.416 --> 00:08:35.708
<b>but there is no advancement in your position,</b>

110
00:08:35.708 --> 00:08:39.083
<b>if you don't get to learn anything new</b>

111
00:08:39.083 --> 00:08:45.250
<b>and all your colleagues get appointed</b>
<b>to higher positions than you,</b>

112
00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:49.500
<b>will you be able to remain satisfied?</b>

113
00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.583
<b>No, right?</b>

114
00:08:50.583 --> 00:08:58.041
<b>Salary is a basic necessity, from which </b>
<b>you can take care of yourself and your family.</b>

115
00:08:58.041 --> 00:09:03.208
<b>But equally important is personal growth</b>

116
00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:08.041
<b>and a constant increase in your work efficiency,</b>

117
00:09:08.041 --> 00:09:12.416
<b>because these also provide you satisfaction.</b>

118
00:09:12.416 --> 00:09:16.375
<b>But are these the only ways to attain fulfillment?</b>

119
00:09:16.375 --> 00:09:21.916
<b>Think about those people who, </b>
<b>along with their professional lives, </b>

120
00:09:21.916 --> 00:09:26.208
<b>also participate in many social service activities.</b>

121
00:09:26.208 --> 00:09:30.541
<b>Trying to have a positive impact with a </b>
<b>sense of duty, on the people around you, </b>

122
00:09:30.541 --> 00:09:37.958
<b>on society, is immensely satisfying.</b>

123
00:09:37.958 --> 00:09:44.708
<b>It gives you a new energy, </b>
<b>awakens a sense of purpose.</b>

124
00:09:44.708 --> 00:09:49.416
<b>And you can participate in such activities </b>
<b>not only in a personal context,</b>

125
00:09:49.416 --> 00:09:53.750
<b>but also in a professional context.</b>

126
00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:57.916
<b>Many organizations nowadays </b>
<b>do social service work,</b>

127
00:09:57.916 --> 00:10:01.791
<b>which you can also join.</b>

128
00:10:01.791 --> 00:10:07.458
<b>Even if that is not the case, </b>
<b>you can still take a personal initiative,</b>

129
00:10:07.458 --> 00:10:11.166
<b>and if you encourage your colleagues,</b>

130
00:10:11.166 --> 00:10:15.291
<b>then surely more people will join you.</b>

131
00:10:15.291 --> 00:10:16.750
<b>Make a start.</b>

132
00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:18.791
<b>Move forward in this direction.</b>

133
00:10:18.791 --> 00:10:20.583
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

